  <prompt>Migrate CreateRecordWizard to consume the shared WizardFollowOns module and delete its local FollowOnSteps/NextStepsStep + SendEmailStep copies. This orchestrator is wrapped by Event/Invoice/KPI wizards, so its follow-ons must come from the shared module.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE shared-UI developer. Follow §11 (no duplicate follow-on impls).</role>
  <goal>CreateRecordWizard renders its Next Steps via WizardFollowOns (declaring its card set as FollowOnCardConfig[]); local FollowOnSteps.tsx + steps duplicates removed; no behavior change for existing wrappers (Matter/Project/Event).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>design §5.9. CreateRecordWizard/FollowOnSteps.tsx is the richest existing copy — 020 generalized it. Its wrappers (CreateEventWizard, CreateProjectWizard) must keep working identically.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/CreateRecordWizard.tsx
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/FollowOnSteps.tsx (delete)
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/steps/ (delete migrated ones)
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WizardFollowOns/
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
